## Lore

The character who falls into this category is a superspy or special operative,
usually working with a secret organization - part of a government, a foreign
government, a secret society, or the low-profile arm of a multimillion dollar
corporation. He may be actively involved with it or no longer affiliated at all.

He is trained in combat, in conventional modern and energy weapons, in espionage
and in covert operations. He may be dedicated to peace, freedom and justice, or
motivated by financial gain.

Do not worry if the superspy''s attributes are not incredibly high. There is more
to this character than natural ability: training and gadgets turn a wimp into a
dynamo.

## GM Notes

**Standing with the organization**, printed 158, decides what equipment reaches
the character and how much money he has. One outcome leaves him black-listed
from further tests but in possession of all his current equipment, to help
establish his alleged innocence - though in the eyes of the law he is a
dangerous criminal. Another makes him a Special Federal Operative on an elite
crimefighting team. As a vigilante he adds 1D4x10,000 dollars to personal
savings; another outcome adds 2D6x1000 to the spy''s.

Hand to hand combat is chosen above rather than granted; every hero gets two
attacks per melee regardless.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-secret-operative');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-secret-operative';

